{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794081711,"nonce":"yR4dQW4Okl9cPlBUq2+wL8bTTXc=","message":"Moved here from doc/design (story a4f7415: design documents are by aspect and describe only what is built; an unbuilt design lives on its issue).\n\n## Story `8ade811` (Bidirectional Jira sync, Jira canonical) — jira-sync.md \"Scope\", deferred to v2\n\nEach was stated as needing no format change in v1:\n\n- sprints (iteration issues, the sprint pass, closed-sprint selection);\n- rank (relative moves through `PUT /agile/1.0/issue/rank`);\n- per-field attribution from the changelog (field imports are authored by the runner today);\n- `components` and `fixVersions`;\n- textarea (ADF) custom fields;\n- `array(user)`, `array(string)`, cascading selects;\n- multi-hop transitions and workflow discovery (today: the one transition whose `to.id` is the target, else pending);\n- degraded discovery (today a forbidden read fails the run);\n- an export scope program (today every unarchived issue of a mapped type is exported);\n- `git work jira link ID KEY`, for issues created without an alias;\n- Starlark bindings, `work.jira.*`, via `host.JiraSync`, one line each\n  (their absence is a gap in AGENTS.md's \"the command line and Starlark are one API\");\n- per-identity Jira credentials;\n- Data Center (REST v2, users by name).\n\nStated as deferred but rejected in the text, so recorded in jira.md's \"Not done\" or elsewhere instead:\n`--watch` (cron is the loop, task `a3a8d16`);\nkey-change aliases (`alias:jira-2`; the link is the Jira id, and Jira resolves old keys).","files":null}]}